            <ArticleTitle>Treatment strategies for bronchial asthma: an update.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>25-6, 29-35</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Advances in understanding the biomolecular basis of the disease's inflammatory and remodeling responses are offering new therapeutic choices--and sometimes new drug-delivery systems--in categories such as beta-agonists, glucocorticoids, and leukotriene blockers. Meanwhile, researchers are exploring novel targets, including intercellular signals and cell-adhesion and gene-activating molecules.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
